# Edge Rover: "When this creature dies, each player creates a Lander token." Bolted, it dies, and Bot1 and Bot2 each
# create one under their own control (CR 111.10u, 101.4): the Rover is in Bot1's graveyard, and the Lander tokens stand
# one on each battlefield. Bot2's Lander is Bot2's to use on Bot2's own turn: {2}, {T}, sacrifice it, search for a basic
# land (Swamp, though Islands remain in the library), tapped. Bot1's own Lander is untouched, still on its battlefield.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Edge Rover
Lightning Bolt
Island x3
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island x5
Island
Swamp
Island x9

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Edge Rover.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
? Bot1.Battlefield.Edge Rover.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Edge Rover)
Bot1.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Lander Token.Types = Artifact
? Bot2.Battlefield.Lander Token.Types = Artifact
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Lander Token.Activate
Bot2.Search(Swamp)
[Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Edge Rover; Lightning Bolt
Bot1.Battlefield = Mox Emerald; Mox Ruby; Lander Token
Bot1.Battlefield.Lander Token.Token = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Lander Token.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Swamp
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Tapped = true
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Library.Count = 9
Bot2.Hand.Count = 6
